      "content": "While framing \"comfort\" as a general patient experience rather than a direct \"better than\" claim can mitigate some compliance risks for the \"Superior\" and \"faster acting\" assertions, FDA guidance still requires precise data supporting any comparative benefit. Since your data only shows a \"slight\" uptick in relief speed, leading with \"Superior Rapid Action\" could be misaligned with the evidence and risk a regulatory warning letter later. You should probably pivot the campaign to focus on \"Advanced Onset and Improved Patient Tolerability\" to accurately reflect the slight improvement while avoiding strict comparative language until specific metrics are verified.",
